\mathrmz^{\mathrm{A}} X \rightarrow_{\mathrm{Z}-$2}^{\mathrm{A}-{ }^{4}$Y+{ }_{2}{ }^{4} \mathrm{He}}
\]<br>Since \( X \) and \( Z \) have same atomic number, that is, same number of protons but different atomic mass, that is, sum of<br>number of protons and neutrons.<br>We know isotopes are atoms with same number of protons but different number of neutrons. Therefore, \( X \) and \( Z \) are<br>isotopes.

